{"q":"283","t":"Move Zeroes","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an integer array <code>nums</code>, move all <code>0</code>&#39;s to the end of it while maintaining the relative order of the non-zero elements.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Note</strong> that you must do this in-place without making a copy of the array.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [0,1,0,3,12]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,3,12,0,0]\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [0]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [0]\n</pre>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>-2<sup>31</sup> &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you minimize the total number of operations done?","h":["<b>In-place</b> means we should not be allocating any space for extra array. But we are allowed to modify the existing array. However, as a first step, try coming up with a solution that makes use of additional space. For this problem as well, first apply the idea discussed using an additional array and the in-place solution will pop up eventually.","A <b>two-pointer</b> approach could be helpful here. The idea would be to have one pointer for iterating the array and another pointer that just works on the non-zero elements of the array."],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"moveZeroes\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"void\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"output\": {\r\n    \"paramindex\": 0\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Two Pointers","slug":"two-pointers"}],"s":[{"t":"Remove Element","s":"remove-element","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Apply Operations to an Array","s":"apply-operations-to-an-array","d":"Easy","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Meta","facebook"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["tcs","tcs"],["Infosys","infosys"],["EPAM Systems","epam-systems"],["Cognizant","cognizant"],["Apple","apple"],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs"],["Chewy","chewy"],["Yandex","yandex"],["Uber","uber"],["Qualcomm","qualcomm"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Accenture","accenture"],["ADP","adp"],["LTIMindtree","lti"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Capgemini","capgemini"],["SAP","sap"],["Cisco","cisco"],["ServiceNow","servicenow"],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs"],["Josh Technology","josh-technology"],["NetApp","netapp"],["PayPal","paypal"],["Samsung","samsung"],["JTG","jtg"],["Anduril","anduril"],["KPMG","kpmg"],["Wix","wix"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",12],["Meta","facebook",10],["Amazon","amazon",6],["Microsoft","microsoft",4],["EPAM Systems","epam-systems",4],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",3],["Infosys","infosys",3],["Cognizant","cognizant",3],["tcs","tcs",2],["Apple","apple",2]],"b":[["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs",2],["Accenture","accenture",2],["Chewy","chewy",2]],"m":[["Yandex","yandex",22],["Zoho","zoho",7],["Oracle","oracle",6],["TikTok","tiktok",5],["Josh Technology","josh-technology",5],["IBM","ibm",4],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs",4],["Capgemini","capgemini",4],["Cisco","cisco",3],["Nvidia","nvidia",3]]}}